# Values come from the environment. In CI these are GitHub Actions secrets;
# locally, export them or use a password manager. Never commit values here.
SECRET_KEY_BASE=$SECRET_KEY_BASE
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=$POSTGRES_PASSWORD
# Composed so the password exists in exactly one place.
#
# Host is the accessory's container name, not 127.0.0.1: the app container
# runs on the "kamal" Docker network (kamal 2.12.0's app command uses
# --network kamal), and accessories join that same network by default. An
# accessory's container name is "<service>-<accessory>" -- with
# service: encounter-engine and the accessory named db, that's
# encounter-engine-db, which Docker's embedded DNS resolves on the shared
# network. 127.0.0.1 from inside the app container is the app container's
# own loopback, where nothing listens on 5432 -- that address only reaches
# the accessory from the host itself (e.g. over an SSH tunnel for admin
# access), never from a sibling container.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://encounter:${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}@encounter-engine-db:5432/encounter_production
SMTP_USERNAME=$SMTP_USERNAME
SMTP_PASSWORD=$SMTP_PASSWORD
# The From address IS the authenticated account, deliberately.
#
# Gmail will not send as an arbitrary address: unless it is a verified
# "Send mail as" alias, Gmail silently rewrites the From header to the
# authenticated account, so a hand-set MAIL_FROM would be quietly ignored.
# And mezin.eu's SPF record authorises Fastmail
# (v=spf1 include:spf.messagingengine.com ?all), not Google — so sending as
# @mezin.eu through Gmail would cost inbox placement even where it was
# honoured. This app forms teams by emailed invitation, so spam-foldering is
# a silent failure that matters.
#
# Deriving it here keeps the address in one place: change the credential and
# the From address follows, with no clear-env copy left to drift.
MAIL_FROM=${SMTP_USERNAME}
KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=$KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD
# Claude API key for superadmin-triggered translation of game content.
# In CI this is a GitHub Actions secret; locally, export it. Never a literal
# here. With this unset the feature is simply absent -- no buttons, no routes
# reachable -- so development and CI need no key at all.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=$ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
